And Other Stories.

So my human Rogue made it to Medusa's after playing ten hours straight
over the weekend. He'd managed to survive so far by training himself up
in the Mines and recovering the bones of his compatriot, who found
great items but was too wimpy to defend himself from a soldier ant.

Amongst the pile of item was a pair of jackboots, which I knew to be
+3. These I wore around, proudly flashing them off as I traversed the
dungeon. But the titan cast destroy armor, and I retreated upstairs
with a pair of sore feet.

Exploring for a few more hours, I still lacked any magic resistance,
and finally decided to take the leap of faith. I went back to Medusa's,
wearing a pair of +0 speed boots, made a hole and jumped right in. I
went through a few more levels and got to the castle, where a master
lich paid me a visit in the mazewalk and cast destroy armor.

Elbereth, with my one wand of lightning, managed to save me, but not my
boots. I slogged on through the castle, crushing the denizens of the
entrance hall with their own drawbridge, and turning the other
occupants to stone. I quickly dashed for the wand of wishing, and
conjured up... speed boots? No, magic resistance and Magicbane were too
important, and I used up the (0:2) wand quickly. The blessed +1 kicking
boots from the storeroom had to do.

Another day of Nethack passed, and I experienced the boredom of pudding
farming. The loot was great, and the spellbooks came in vast numbers
from my pudding-hungry god. I even managed to get a throughly-burnt and
-rotted pair of speed boots from Gehennom enchanted up to blessed
fireproof +4. So I went downstairs to read, and accidentally eyed the
scroll of enchant armor in my inventory.

Your speed boots glow violently for a moment, then vaporize! You feel
yourself slow down a bit.

Oh well. Hopefully my current pair of speed boots will last.

