And Other Stories

So I was pudding farming up in dungeon level ten. It's a great place,
really, once it's all dug out and lit. I think it's a piece of art: On
the left wall there's a large emptied shop, to teleport to if the
puddings overflow. The up-stairs are encased in their private room. The
old rooms are decorated with statues of Kops that the old shopkeeper
summoned, and one room is half-dug out, as my decorative temple.

After many hours of drudgery, I managed to forumlate a grand method of
farming. On the altar, I read an blessed scroll of earth, to produce
this:

000
0_0
000

As the staircase was in the lower right hand corner, I made it my
desired exit, and struck that boulder:

000
0_0
00>

At this stage, only one pudding would bother me, and I would see many
less messages from the world around me. But my view still wasn't
completely blocked. So I used a few boulders lying around the level
left over from some rock-eaters, and pushed them into place. (Through a
sea of puddings, no less. My right hand probably has carpal tunnel by
now.)

000
0_0
00>0
##00

Now both puddings and I can move about or go downstairs with ease, and
I only have to see and fight one at the same time! (If anyone wants my
save-file, just email me.)

Ok, enough of strategy. Let's have some humour, eh?
I name the puddings various things, just to keep myself sane. I still
laugh at the message I got when accidentally pushing a boulder with
monster-detection on:
"There's clean-shaven goodness on the other side. -more-"

Likewise, when I went downstairs (there are two holes on the farm
level, from some creatures that escaped me... it often leaks puddings!)
and into a closet to read spellbooks:
"Clean-shaven goodness oozes under the door. You stop studying."

No, no, not THAT sort of clean-shaven... it's a joke about a bearded
history professor. Keep your minds out of the gutter; there's brown
puddings there!

Speaking of puddings, there was also a sink on the level below the
altar. I managed to produce a black pudding this way, but how should I
get it up? Fortunately, I had procured a spellbook of charm monster by
now, and with the robe I was wearing, I could get a decent, if not 100%
success rate. So I charmed the black pudding, magic-whistled it up to
the staircase (I had actually lured the untame pudding to the staircase
to see if it would follow me up. No such luck.), and beat it into
wildness. I had to do this twice, as I slew the first one with my
throughly corroded -3 knife named Breadknife.

Speaking of Breadknife, my first -3 Breadknife became the blessed
rustproof +1 Breadknife when I prayed while wielding it. A historical
artifact, indeed!

